        <li>[about:night] {GOD}, the night's coming, and we're here to meet it.</li>
        <li>[about:dead] {GOD}, we remember the ones who aren't with us any more.</li>
        <li>[olde] Gather ye, all, for this is the week's hour of {GOD}.</li>
        <li>[olde] {GOD}, {GODEPITHET}, another week is past, and we are come again before thee.</li>
        <li>[olde] Sit ye down, every one, and hear what {GOD} hath given us this week.</li>
        <li>[olde] Unto {GOD} we give this hour, as we give it every week.</li>
        <li>[olde,priest] Hear ye the word of {GOD}, as it was spoken unto our fathers.</li>
        <li>[olde,about:harvest] {GOD}, thou hast kept the field this week, and we give thee thanks.</li>
        <li>[olde,about:hearth] The fire is lit and the week's work done, {GOD}, so sit thou with us.</li>
        <li>[olde,about:waters] {GOD}, for the water drawn this week we give thee thanks.</li>
