  <!-- ===================== A believer asks for a place (A8) ===================== -->
  <ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_Dlm_PlaceAsked</defName>
    <label>a place for a god</label>
    <workerClass>ColonyCouncil.DilemmaWorker_PlaceAsked</workerClass>
    <weight>0.8</weight>
    <cooldownDays>25</cooldownDays>
    <minColonists>3</minColonists>
    <texts>
      <li>{A_nameDef} has prayed to {GOD} wherever {A_pronoun} happens to stand for long enough, and asks the council for a place of {GOD}'s own at this home: an altar, a statue, a stone, whatever the colony can spare. {A_nameDef} would say the words there.</li>
      <li>{A_nameDef} came to the council with a quiet request. Every god the colony keeps has a corner, {A_pronoun} says, except {GOD}. Would the council give {GOD} a place?</li>
      <li>[lowtech] {A_nameDef} has found a stone {A_pronoun} thinks would do, and asks the council whether {GOD} may have it, and the ground it stands on.</li>
      <li>[priest] {A_nameDef} reminds the council that {GOD} has believers here and no place to be prayed to, and would like that put right.</li>
    </texts>
    <defaultOption>0</defaultOption>
    <options>
      <li>
        <label>Give {GOD} a place here</label>
        <outcome>The council agreed that {GOD} should have a place at this home. {A_nameDef} thanked them, and will say the words at whatever place the colony gives.</outcome>
        <ways><tradition>1</tradition><openness>1</openness></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_PlaceAgreed" />
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>A</target><amount>1</amount></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>Not now</label>
        <outcome>The council said not now. {A_nameDef} nodded and said nothing more about it.</outcome>
        <ways><toil>1</toil></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>A</target><thought>Rimfolk_Worship_PlaceRefused</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_GodFavour"><god>1</god><amount>-1</amount><source>Neglect</source><offence>Neglect</offence><why>the council gave {GOD} no place</why></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>A</target><amount>-1</amount></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
    </options>
  </ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>

  <!-- ===================== Whose feast this season (B6) ===================== -->
  <ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_Dlm_RivalFeasts</defName>
    <label>two feasts in one season</label>
    <workerClass>ColonyCouncil.DilemmaWorker_RivalFeasts</workerClass>
    <weight>0.9</weight>
    <cooldownDays>30</cooldownDays>
    <minColonists>4</minColonists>
    <roleB />
    <texts>
      <li>Two feasts fall this season, {GOD}'s and {GOD2}'s, and the two gods have never been able to stand each other. {A_nameDef} wants {GOD}'s kept in full, {B_nameDef} wants {GOD2}'s, and both say the colony can't afford two feasts and two sets of guests in one season.</li>
      <li>{A_nameDef} and {B_nameDef} have been arguing about the season's feasts since breakfast. {GOD}'s or {GOD2}'s: one gets the offering and the guests, the other is kept quietly. The council is asked to settle it.</li>
      <li>[lowtech] There's one season, two feasts, and enough food for one. {A_nameDef} speaks for {GOD}, {B_nameDef} for {GOD2}.</li>
    </texts>
    <defaultOption>2</defaultOption>
    <options>
      <li>
        <label>{GOD}'s feast in full; {GOD2}'s kept quietly</label>
        <outcome>The council gave the season to {GOD}. {B_nameDef} said {GOD2}'s people would keep their feast anyway, just quietly.</outcome>
        <ways><tradition>1</tradition></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_FeastFirst"><god>1</god></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>A</target><amount>1</amount></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>B</target><amount>-1</amount></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>{GOD2}'s feast in full; {GOD}'s kept quietly</label>
        <outcome>The council gave the season to {GOD2}. {A_nameDef} said {GOD}'s people would keep their feast anyway, just quietly.</outcome>
        <ways><tradition>1</tradition></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_FeastFirst"><god>2</god></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>B</target><amount>1</amount></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>A</target><amount>-1</amount></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>Both in full</label>
        <outcome>The council said both feasts would be kept in full, offerings, guests and all. The stores will feel it, and some say neither god likes sharing a season.</outcome>
        <ways><generosity>2</generosity><toil>-1</toil></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_GodFavour"><god>1</god><amount>-2</amount><onlyJealous>true</onlyJealous><source>Neglect</source><offence>Rivals</offence><why>a season shared with {GOD2}</why></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_GodFavour"><god>2</god><amount>-2</amount><onlyJealous>true</onlyJealous><source>Neglect</source><offence>Rivals</offence><why>a season shared with {GOD}</why></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
    </options>
  </ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>

</Defs>
